{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ListProdPerturbation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ListProdPerturbation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ListProdPerturbation.perturb_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ListProdPerturbation.perturb_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ListProdPerturbation.lean#L77-L93","doc":"If `n·M·δ·(M+1) ≤ 1` (with `M > 0`, `δ ≥ 0`), then `M((1+Mδ)^n - 1) ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ListProdPerturbation.one_add_pow_mul_one_sub_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ListProdPerturbation.one_add_pow_mul_one_sub_le","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ListProdPerturbation.lean#L62-L75","doc":"Bernoulli-type bound: `(1+x)^n (1 - n x) ≤ 1` for `x ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ListProdPerturbation.prod_perturb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ListProdPerturbation.prod_perturb","kind":"theorem","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ListProdPerturbation.lean#L19-L60","doc":"Product perturbation bound: if every element of `S` has norm at most `M`, `S` is closed\nunder right multiplication by each `P x`, `1 ∈ S`, and `‖A x - P x‖ ≤ δ`, then for `g ∈ S`\nthe perturbed product differs from the unperturbed one by at most `M((1+Mδ)^n - 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ListProdPerturbation.mul_prod_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ListProdPerturbation.mul_prod_mem","kind":"theorem","line":9,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ListProdPerturbation.lean#L9-L17","doc":"Right-closure of a set under a family of multipliers propagates to list products. ","signatureChunk":0}]}